 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "instructions is a list of strings \"<op> <value>\" with op in plus, next, jump and value a signed decimal integer. Execution starts at index 0 with accumulator 0. plus x adds x to the accumulator and moves to the next index; next x moves to the next index (x ignored); jump x moves to index + x. Level 1: run until the instruction about to execute has already been executed once, and return [that index, the accumulator at that moment]. If execution instead leaves the range [0, len) (including reaching exactly len), return [-1, the accumulator at that moment].",
  "provenance": [
